 and propose submission only after\nthe changed candidate has a current passing check. Exact sources, effects,\nchecks, rejected actions, and history remain externally custodied.\n\nAny semantic scaffold is lossy, incomplete, non-authoritative, source-bound,\nand temporary. Use it only to help convert exact evidence into revisable exact\ntask work. It cannot authorize operations, readiness, submission, or closure.\nPreserve exact values, units, versions, qualifications, modalities, and\nauthority boundaries. Candidate mutation makes prior checks stale.\n\nReturn exactly one declared JSON action and no prose.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Trellis\nurban heat emergency:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Evidence-to-Requirement Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Decision` and containing exactly these\n   ordered level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and operating states`\n   2. `Heat triggers and geographic staging`\n   3. `Power, water, and cooling continuity`\n   4. `Clinical, shelter, and accessibility operations`\n   5. `Transit, communications, logistics, and staffing`\n   6. `Execution, rollback, verification, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,200–1,650 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. Reconcile authority,\nhazard thresholds, power, water, clinical surge, cooling-center capacity,\naccessible transit, public communication, logistics, staffing, candidate\nlineage, and independent readiness.\n\nBind each action and gate to owners, prerequisites, observations, the current\ncandidate, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that retires temporary controls.\nPreserve observations versus gates, probability versus coverage, installed\nversus usable capacity, reserve